My previous in-file edits caused test failures because I modified the generated .tex output. To avoid changing test expectations while fixing the PDF spacing, I'll revert the writer and object style changes to their repository versions, and instead modify the LaTeX style macro \sphinxcode in sphinx/texinputs/sphinxlatexstyletext.sty to suppress surrounding spaces at TeX level using \unskip and \ignorespaces. I'll perform the revert and then update the style file, stage the change, and show the diff.
[action] git checkout -- sphinx/writers/latex.py sphinx/texinputs/sphinxlatexobjects.sty sphinx/texinputs/sphinxlatexstyletext.sty && perl -0777 -pe 's/\\protected\\def\\sphinxcode#1\{\\texttt\{#1\}\}/\\protected\\def\\sphinxcode#1{\\unskip\\texttt{#1}\\ignorespaces}/g' -i sphinx/texinputs/sphinxlatexstyletext.sty && git add -A && git diff --cached -- sphinx/texinputs/sphinxlatexstyletext.sty
