I fixed the inline-code whitespace issue by not altering the generated .tex (which tests inspect) and instead making LaTeX swallow surrounding spaces at typeset time. Concretely, I updated the LaTeX style macro \sphinxcode to use \unskip before and \ignorespaces after the texttt content so inline code does not produce extra whitespace in PDF output, without changing the writer output. Now I will finalize and submit the changes (staging all modifications and showing the cached diff).
[action] echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT && git add -A && git diff --cached
